WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.828 --> 00:00:14.272
No one, not even Jo herself, could deny that she had a short temper.

2
00:00:15.132 --> 00:00:21.814
That however, normally meant that whatever angered her was quickly forgotten, and the good-natured Jo prevailed once again.

3
00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:24.495
But this time was a different matter.

4
00:00:25.556 --> 00:00:32.152
Nothing anyone said, not even Mother's tender comforting words, could soothe the burning pain in Jo's heart.

5
00:00:32.172 --> 00:00:38.437
"I will never forgive her," Jo sobbed into Mother's arms.

6
00:00:39.678 --> 00:00:45.663
"I know you are very angry at this moment," Mother sympathized, "but don't utter words you may regret

7
00:00:45.723 --> 00:00:50.127
later." Inside, Mother's heart wept with her second child.

8
00:00:51.147 --> 00:00:56.692
Jo's beauty and charm, unlike Meg's or Amy's, was not immediately obvious to others.

9
00:00:57.708 --> 00:01:02.009
Her strength came from deep inside her creative soul and shone in her writing.

10
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:08.731
This particular story was even more important to Jo because it was dedicated to her father.

11
00:01:09.792 --> 00:01:15.333
To Jo, taking and destroying her story was the same as cold-heartedly stabbing her in the back then

12
00:01:15.413 --> 00:01:16.514
cruelly laughing at her.

13
00:01:16.534 --> 00:01:24.436
"Even if I forgive Amy," Jo sniffed, "I don't think I will ever forget what she did."

14
00:01:25.948 --> 00:01:31.513
Mother held Jo close and silently prayed that this matter would not ruin the relationship between her two

15
00:01:31.573 --> 00:01:32.334
daughters forever.

16
00:01:33.795 --> 00:01:37.158
For the next couple of days Jo avoided Amy altogether.

17
00:01:38.419 --> 00:01:43.884
When they happened to come across each other, perhaps at mealtimes, Jo stared at her coldly and moved

18
00:01:43.924 --> 00:01:46.386
away as if Amy had some contagious disease.

19
00:01:47.908 --> 00:01:52.352
Amy found this chilly treatment far more painful than being slapped or pinched by her sister.

20
00:01:53.276 --> 00:01:58.299
On several occasions Amy tried to catch Jo off guard when she happened to be in a somewhat

21
00:01:58.339 --> 00:01:59.980
good mood or at least smiling.

22
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:07.944
Each time, however, she was unsuccessful because Jo immediately stiffened and cooled when she saw Amy anywhere near

23
00:02:07.984 --> 00:02:13.147
her. One afternoon, Laurie came over to cheer up his downhearted buddy.

24
00:02:13.907 --> 00:02:20.211
At first Jo refused to accept what Laurie called his "special remedy" for the troubled heart─a good cry,

25
00:02:20.351 --> 00:02:21.792
a good laugh, and a good friend.

26
00:02:23.168 --> 00:02:27.029
But later she changed her mind when she realized that Laurie did make her happier.

27
00:02:27.049 --> 00:02:30.810
"See? It's not too difficult to smile, is it?"

28
00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:32.031
Laurie teased.

29
00:02:32.871 --> 00:02:39.313
"I'm not smiling; I'm frowning because you're making my head ache," Jo muttered, turning her head away to

30
00:02:39.373 --> 00:02:41.353
hide the corners of her mouth turning upward.

31
00:02:41.373 --> 00:02:43.754
"I have just the thing for headaches!"

32
00:02:44.194 --> 00:02:47.855
Laurie shot his finger up as if he had just thought of a brilliant idea.

33
00:02:47.875 --> 00:02:51.320
"Oh no," moaned Jo.

34
00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:55.841
"With all your remedies, you should be a doctor; not an artist, when you grow up, dear boy."

35
00:02:56.782 --> 00:03:00.763
Flapping his hand to silence her, Laurie simply said, "Fresh air."

36
00:03:00.783 --> 00:03:04.003
"I beg your pardon?"

37
00:03:04.324 --> 00:03:04.964
Jo laughed.

38
00:03:05.824 --> 00:03:08.425
"You need fresh air to get rid of that headache!

39
00:03:09.105 --> 00:03:12.486
And I know the best place for it," Laurie nodded knowingly.

40
00:03:12.506 --> 00:03:14.726
"Whatever you say, Dr.

41
00:03:14.786 --> 00:03:17.067
Laurie," replied the obedient patient.

42
00:03:17.087 --> 00:03:23.062
"Get your skates and meet me at my house," said Laurie, as he reached for the door handle.

43
00:03:23.983 --> 00:03:24.724
"Oh, skating!

44
00:03:25.264 --> 00:03:26.585
Why didn't I think of that!

45
00:03:27.286 --> 00:03:28.627
I'll be over in two seconds!"

46
00:03:29.448 --> 00:03:32.290
Jo clapped her hands excitedly and ran out of the room.

47
00:03:33.772 --> 00:03:38.456
If Jo had turned around as she crossed the living room, she would have caught sight of Amy,

48
00:03:38.836 --> 00:03:43.100
pretending to be interested in a book, but secretly listening to their conversation.

49
00:03:44.741 --> 00:03:47.464
Jo, however, was too excited to notice anything.

50
00:03:48.592 --> 00:03:53.496
In the woods behind the March house and Laurence mansion was a pond that froze over every winter.

51
00:03:54.457 --> 00:03:56.899
Some years it was even safe to skate on.

52
00:03:56.919 --> 00:04:01.824
"Brookes says the ice may not be thick enough in the middle but we should be able to

53
00:04:01.884 --> 00:04:04.146
skate along the edges," Laurie pointed out.

54
00:04:04.166 --> 00:04:06.047
"I'm not afraid.

55
00:04:06.087 --> 00:04:06.528
Are you?"

56
00:04:06.848 --> 00:04:07.428
Jo asked.

57
00:04:07.448 --> 00:04:15.275
"Of course not," Laurie replied hotly, "but we should be careful because the water will be freezing cold

58
00:04:15.295 --> 00:04:15.956
if you fall in."

59
00:04:17.104 --> 00:04:19.465
Jo tied the laces on her skates and stood up.

60
00:04:19.485 --> 00:04:22.045
"I'll race you around the pond.

61
00:04:22.406 --> 00:04:24.046
Loser has to carry the winner home!"

62
00:04:24.966 --> 00:04:27.927
With that Jo sped off, letting out a loud yell.

63
00:04:28.607 --> 00:04:31.348
Laurie hurriedly tied his laces and shot after her.

64
00:04:32.208 --> 00:04:38.110
Amy was relieved to see Jo behaving more like her usual self, though she still disapproved of her

65
00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:39.790
sister's tomboyish ways.

66
00:04:40.531 --> 00:04:44.992
Amy quickly put on her skates, determined to corner Jo while Laurie was around.

67
00:04:46.024 --> 00:04:50.248
She felt confident that this would be the day that Jo would forgive her so they could be

68
00:04:50.268 --> 00:04:51.309
at peace once again.

69
00:04:51.329 --> 00:04:56.393
"Jo!" she called out to the small figures on the opposite side of the pond.

70
00:04:57.113 --> 00:05:02.958
Hearing her name, Jo looked up but when she saw who was calling, her smile quickly turned into

71
00:05:02.998 --> 00:05:03.539
a scowl.

72
00:05:04.239 --> 00:05:07.382
She stopped abruptly, nearly causing Laurie to crash into her.

73
00:05:08.543 --> 00:05:09.264
"What's the matter?"

74
00:05:09.764 --> 00:05:11.025
Laurie cried breathlessly.

75
00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:14.048
"What is she doing here?"

76
00:05:14.564 --> 00:05:18.667
Jo pointed irritably to her sister who waved while trying to balance on her skates.

77
00:05:19.807 --> 00:05:23.089
Amy wobbled on her feet and carefully stepped onto the icy pond.

78
00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:28.612
Unfortunately for her, she hadn't heard Laurie's warnings about the middle of the pond.

79
00:05:29.633 --> 00:05:35.816
Wanting to reach Jo and Laurie as quickly as possible, Amy began to skate toward them, cutting across

80
00:05:35.876 --> 00:05:36.917
the center of the pond.

81
00:05:36.937 --> 00:05:38.878
"Oh no!

82
00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:39.879
Amy! Stop!

83
00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:40.939
Don't skate there!"

84
00:05:41.259 --> 00:05:41.920
Laurie shouted.

85
00:05:42.736 --> 00:05:45.518
Amy could not hear exactly what Laurie was shouting.

86
00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:48.221
Her only focus was on reaching Jo.

87
00:05:48.241 --> 00:05:50.923
"Amy! Stop!

88
00:05:51.303 --> 00:05:52.984
Go around the edge of the pond!"

89
00:05:53.465 --> 00:05:55.547
Jo cried, swinging her arms frantically.

90
00:05:56.307 --> 00:06:01.511
What happened next occurred in a flash, but to Jo everything seemed in slow motion.

91
00:06:02.632 --> 00:06:07.796
Amy tilted forward as if she had tripped over something, then she glanced down and immediately jerked her

92
00:06:07.836 --> 00:06:09.718
head up, searching for an escape.

93
00:06:11.019 --> 00:06:15.567
Jo heard a slight cracking noise like distant thunder, followed by a splash.

94
00:06:15.587 --> 00:06:22.732
"Amy!" Jo screamed as she saw her sister disappear rapidly beneath the icy waters.

95
00:06:24.274 --> 00:06:29.598
Everything that had happened between her and Amy vanished from Jo's thoughts as the only fear that gripped

96
00:06:29.638 --> 00:06:32.981
her now was that she might never see her little sister again.

97
00:06:33.861 --> 00:06:39.026
Jo started to skate toward the hole Amy had fallen into, but Laurie grabbed her before she could

98
00:06:39.066 --> 00:06:39.806
go any further.

99
00:06:39.826 --> 00:06:45.070
"It's too dangerous," he spun his head around and located a large fallen branch.

100
00:06:46.291 --> 00:06:47.051
"Help me with this!"

101
00:06:48.092 --> 00:06:52.634
Laurie and Jo got the branch and carefully skated closer to where Amy's head was bobbing in and

102
00:06:52.694 --> 00:06:53.335
out of the water.

103
00:06:54.395 --> 00:06:55.696
"Amy! Grab this!

104
00:06:55.976 --> 00:06:56.937
We'll pull you out!"

105
00:06:57.297 --> 00:07:00.599
Jo yelled as she and Laurie pushed the branch toward the hole.

106
00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:06.703
Somehow Amy heard her sister's instructions and grasped the branch with her cold, weak hands.

107
00:07:06.723 --> 00:07:08.824
"Hold tightly!"

108
00:07:09.224 --> 00:07:13.046
Laurie shouted, as he and Jo pulled Amy out of the freezing waters.

109
00:07:13.907 --> 00:07:20.090
When they had gotten Amy to safer ground, Jo threw her own coat over Amy's shivering little body.

110
00:07:20.931 --> 00:07:25.993
Laurie did the same, even taking off his wool sweater and covering Amy's head with it.

111
00:07:26.013 --> 00:07:28.515
"We have to get her home, now!"

112
00:07:28.895 --> 00:07:31.336
Laurie said in an unusually authoritative voice.

113
00:07:32.057 --> 00:07:33.938
Jo was not about to argue with her friend.

114
00:07:34.758 --> 00:07:40.108
She was glad that someone was taking charge of the situation, because she had never felt so helpless

115
00:07:40.289 --> 00:07:40.990
in all her life.
